  "about": "The observation of the local desktop in its wire form (the JSON every binding exchanges): a surface, permission or accessibility case gives one snapshot object and whether it is valid; a binding decodes it into its own model and validates it, and a snapshot that does not decode (a field of the wrong type) is invalid too. An options case builds the limits (zero is not a case: Go reads it as the default) and reports invalid or accepts them. Permission states are ready, denied, not-determined, not-required, unsupported and unavailable, and the reason rules of capability/v1 apply to unsupported and unavailable. Timestamps are RFC 3339. A display or window scale of 0 is written by leaving scale out.",
